  "body": "For `AudioTrackList` and `VideoTrackList`, the spec says to 'queue a task to fire a simple event' when a `change` event is indicated, but for `TextTrackList` there is no specific description of when to fire the event. In particular, it should be specified that the event is fired from a queued task, rather than synchronously.\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-texttracklist-item\n\n> textTrack . mode [ =​ value ]\n> \n> ```\n> Returns the text track mode, represented by a string from the following list:​\n> \n> \"disabled\"\n> \n>     The text track disabled mode\\.\n> \"hidden\"\n> \n>     The text track hidden mode\\.\n> \"showing\"\n> \n>     The text track showing mode\\.\n> \n> Can be set, to change the mode\\.\n> ```\n",
